One into many forms is known as polymorphism. 
polymorphism is classified into two parts:
          1)Method Overloading.
          2)Method Overriding.
Method Overloading:- 
   Note :- In python latest function definations will get executed . And in python method overloading is not possible directly . if we want to get method overload error we need to use the concept of default parameters . 
def fun1(a,b):
    print(a,b) 

def fun1(a = 0,b = 0,c = 0):
    print(a,b,c) 
    
fun1(10,20) 

MethodOverride:- 
class SoftwareTrainer:
    def resignation(self):
        print("SoftwareTrainer wanna resign") 

class HardwareTrainer(SoftwareTrainer):
    def resignation(self):
        print("HardwareTrainer wanna resign")
        super().resignation() # to get parent class properties 

ob = HardwareTrainer() 
ob.resignation() 
